From ad7b93f3fbbc4cceebd27d3783b2a3852f1343f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 20:39:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Implement XEP-0421 occupant identifiers in MUC rooms

Add the `occupant_id` option to mod_muc. When it is enabled, rooms add an
<occupant-id xmlns='urn:xmpp:occupant-id:0'/> element to the presences,
group chat messages and private messages they reflect, replacing any such
element sent by the client. The ID is an HMAC of the occupant's real bare
JID with a random per-room salt, which is stored with persistent rooms, so
it is stable across rejoins and nick changes and does not reveal the JID.
Rooms and the MUC service advertise the feature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01ETaRHXo1LmPHqZB9SXMucM
